## 4. The Frontier Model Family: Tradeoffs & Selection Matrix

Navigating OpenAI’s model ecosystem requires understanding the structural engineering tradeoffs between latency, compute cost, modality, and deep cognitive reasoning capability. In modern enterprise architecture, routing 100% of queries to a single flagship model is an operational anti-pattern that guarantees excessive cloud expenditures and unacceptable user latency.

<div class="diagram-container">
  <img src="../assets/svg/diag_ch01_model_family_tradeoffs.svg" alt="Model Family Tradeoff Matrix" />
  <p class="diagram-caption">Figure 1.4: Model Family Tradeoff Matrix: Balancing Latency, Ingestion Cost, Multimodal Vision, and Recursive Reasoning</p>
</div>

### 4.1 GPT-4o: The Multimodal Omnichannel Flagship
GPT-4o represents the pinnacle of unified multimodal intelligence. Engineered as a high-throughput, low-latency flagship model, it processes text, high-resolution imagery, video frames, and audio waveforms in a single end-to-end forward pass.
* **Latency Profile**: Balanced, generating tokens at approximately 80–110 tokens per second with a Time-To-First-Token (TTFT) under 1.2 seconds.
* **Context Capacity**: 128,000 input tokens, up to 16,384 output completion tokens.
* **Primary Strengths**: Complex Custom GPT actions, multi-turn conversational synthesis, sandboxed Python Code Interpreter execution, native vision analysis, structured JSON extraction, and sophisticated enterprise workflow orchestration.

### 4.2 GPT-4o-mini: The High-Throughput Volume Workhorse
Announced as the replacement for GPT-3.5 Turbo, GPT-4o-mini delivers near-flagship intelligence at an astonishing 60% lower latency and 90% lower economic cost.
* **Latency Profile**: Ultra-low, generating tokens at 140–180 tokens per second with TTFT under 400 milliseconds.
* **Cost Structure**: $0.15 per 1 million input tokens; $0.60 per 1 million output tokens.
* **Primary Strengths**: High-volume document classification, customer service triage routing, preliminary email drafting, programmatic entity extraction, real-time autocomplete backends, and cascading fallback verification in multi-agent swarms.

### 4.3 OpenAI o1: The Autonomous Reasoning Model
OpenAI o1 represents a fundamental architectural departure from standard autoregressive predictors. Rather than immediately generating output tokens, o1 executes a hidden internal **Chain-of-Thought (CoT)** reasoning loop before emitting a single user-facing character.

The model generates hundreds or thousands of private reasoning tokens where it actively plans its approach, attempts different algorithmic paths, checks intermediate mathematical assertions, scores potential solutions, catches its own logical errors, and backtracks when a dead-end is reached.
* **Latency Profile**: Deliberate and contemplative, with response times ranging from 5 seconds to over 45 seconds depending on problem complexity.
* **Cost Structure**: Premium tier ($15.00 per 1M input / $60.00 per 1M output).
* **Primary Strengths**: Competitive programming, complex mathematical theorem proofs, multi-file code refactoring, distributed consensus architecture design, cryptographic audits, and high-stakes legal contract analysis where zero error tolerance is required.

